{"name":"Lucidity","hex":"#1e4469","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lucidity","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The property of being lucid; lucidness.","The state of being aware that one is dreaming, i.e. being in a lucid dream."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lucidity"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lucidity (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Lucidity is the debut studio album by the Dutch symphonic metal band Delain. It was released on 4 September 2006 by Roadrunner Records. It was released in the US by Sensory Records on 22 June 2010. After the disbandment of the band which had recorded the Amenity demo, the keyboard player and main composer Martijn Westerholt decided to retain lead vocalist Charlotte Wessels and to record an album with the best session musicians available, without the perspective of bringing the songs on tour. He recruited for the project Marko Hietala on vocals and bass, Ad Sluijter, Guus Eikens and Jan Yrlund on guitars and Ariën van Weesenbeek on drums. Guest vocalists on the album were Sharon den Adel, Liv Kristine, and George Oosthoek."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a5/Lucidity_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucidity_(album)","wikidata":"Q1934246"},{"title":"Lucidity (festival)","blocks":[{"text":"Lucidity was an annual, three-day transformational festival in Santa Barbara, California. Its final installment was in 2023, following the cancellation of its planned 2024 event."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bb/Lucidity_festival_logo2015.jpg/330px-Lucidity_festival_logo2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucidity_(festival)","wikidata":"Q6696937"},{"title":"Lucidity (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lucidity\" is a song by Tame Impala, released as a single in 2010. It was recorded during the sessions for the Innerspeaker album in 2009, and released as the second single from that album. The single features artwork from Australian artist Leif Podhajsky, who also created the artwork for Innerspeaker and the follow-up Lonerism. \"Lucidity\" came in at number 74 in the Triple J Hottest 100 in 2010."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e9/Tame_Impala_Lucidity_single_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucidity_(song)","wikidata":"Q6696939"},{"title":"Lucidity (web series)","blocks":[{"text":"Lucidity: The Web Saga is a metaphysical comedy web series produced by Third Productions. The program was created and written by Sean Oliver and Danny Torgersen, who co-star as George (Torgersen) and Jason (Oliver). In addition to screening at the 2013 Phoenix Comicon, Lucidity was an Official Selection at the L.A. Web Series Festival in 2011, 2012, and 2013. Winning The Saga multiple awards in Directing, Editing, Composition, and Special Effects"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucidity_(web_series)","wikidata":"Q6696942"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Sharon_den_Adel_Earthshaker_Fest.jpg/500px-Sharon_den_Adel_Earthshaker_Fest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Sharon_den_Adel_Earthshaker_Fest.jpg/500px-Sharon_den_Adel_Earthshaker_Fest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASharon_den_Adel_Earthshaker_Fest.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Marco-Hietala.JPG/500px-Marco-Hietala.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Marco-Hietala.JPG/500px-Marco-Hietala.JPG?utm_source=en.wi